A||N||8||grinthock||Import Fest Pics 2001 Skydome||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||09-29-2001||04:58 PM||||Just got back from ImportFest 2001 at skydome.  Some new Subaru, MR2, and some domestic stuff, lots of imports, which isn't an issue, I like them too.<P>Took lots of pics located at<BR> <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/importfest/" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/importfest/</A> <P>It was a good show, some neat stuff, saw a Golf GTI with 2 VR6's one in the front and one in the BACK!  Some Hydro suspension jobs, the 2nd Glance was there.<P>PS2's GALORE in cars, along with DVD, and audio stuff.  ALOT of chop jobs.  <P>what bugged me the most is when people pull their dash trim out, paint it with a damn paint brush then try to stick it back on with scotch TAPE!  it was so common.<P>Anyway check out the pics in that gallery.. htere is 132 of them<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||09-29-2001||06:40 PM||||I don't get it.<BR>People are allowed to have a hobby, but I'm allowed to have an opinion about it.  Besides the fact that I didn't understand what I was looking at in many of those pics, it seemed to me that for the most part people were taking stupid cars and making them even more stupid.<P>Why was the cotton placed around the tires of that car?  To make it look like they were smoking?  That gives me ideas which involve dry ice...<P>||||reg||5
Z||000002||Leper||09-29-2001||09:10 PM||||The P000 prefixes on the picutes were coincidental, but funny nonetheless.<P>I liked the like green Bimmer, the NSX's and the 2 decked out mustangs in this pic <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/importfest/cwdata/P000778.html" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/importfest/cwdata/P000778.html</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||09-29-2001||11:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>Why was the cotton placed around the tires of that car?  To make it look like they were smoking?  That gives me ideas which involve dry ice...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Usually see that done at lowrider shows.  I haven't done the research into the origins of cotton in the wheelwells for many obvious reasons, I guess it's supposed to make your car really cool!<P>Maybe I'll try it with my Fiero at the next show.  Uh, NOT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><P>Thanks for posting the pics grinthock<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000004||grinthock||09-29-2001||11:32 PM||||Hey thanks guys, no problem on the pics, yeah that cotton thing is STUPID, that's why I took a pic of it... Like the NSX?  One of those pics was the one I took WAY later in the day after I left, it was on the street.  <P>Some nice stuff there, I liked that GTP.||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||09-29-2001||11:35 PM||||Yeah well I was walking through Nathan Phillips Square in Toronto and got a pic of these 2 cops working Riot duty at a demonstration at city hall, they were demonstrating the use of force against Afganistan.  <P>The first pic is FieroMatt (my bro) on the toronto SkyWalk.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B>The P000 prefixes on the picutes were coincidental, but funny nonetheless.<P>I liked the like green Bimmer, the NSX's and the 2 decked out mustangs in this pic <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/importfest/cwdata/P000778.html" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/importfest/cwdata/P000778.html</A> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
